  ('zcrm_1579374000179049560', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083756038', 'Lisa Birkhofer', NULL, '1-20-26 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Disenrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Lisa BIRKHOFER</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Select Health Value Silver $3400 Medical Deductible</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$100</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$3,300</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 01/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>$49.04 /month </b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">after $1,200.76 financial help</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Exchange policy number:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 6709530128</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Coverage dates:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 01/01/26 - 01/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Last updated:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 11/08/25</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-20 17:43:57', '2026-01-20 17:43:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179049555', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083756038', 'Lisa Birkhofer', NULL, '1-20-26 Lisa was curious what would happen if she moved some money from IRA to Roth IRA and how it would impact her C4 plan. She wants to move $45K which would then be added to her $27,684 SS income. That would bring her above the threshold of gaining an APTC. Therefore, she would have to pay $1200.76 for her current C4 plan. So, I explained Premium Care since she doesn''t have any selfe-emplpyment income. She does her wellness screenings but doesn''t need a colonoscopy until she''s 70. She doesn''t love mammos but does them. She''s on the fence about a pap and is happy to forgeo it. She did a surgery for glaucoma in 2025 and it''s good to go. She does check ups but thinks she was being taken advantage of with the numerous check ups since her levels were showing up as good. Now she just has dry eyes. Her parents are alive and well still too!  She chose Premium Care $1000/$299 and I cancelled her Select Health plan and sent her proof from her C4 account. She had no idea that she has other options outside of ACA. She''s very happy to join this until she moves to Medicare in 2 years.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-20 17:43:21', '2026-01-20 17:43:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179049550', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176137034', 'Clara Pickell', NULL, '1-20-26 Clara is trying to update her payment since it didn''t go through. But, she''s been trying for a few days to call without success. I gave her <span style="">844-580-2474 to try which is Benefit Health Plan Inc. She''ll try that. If that doesn''t work, I''ll find out where to send her next.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-20 16:48:40', '2026-01-20 16:48:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000179049545', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165442', 'Olivia & Craig Brown', NULL, '1-20-26 Craig remove me as his broker on C4. I called and spoke with Olivia. She took my name and number. She said he''s on the phone possibly with C4 right now. Hopefully he''ll call me back for help.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-20 15:23:06', '2026-01-20 15:23:06'),
