  ('zcrm_1579374000178551064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178551069', 'Matthew Hogan', NULL, '1-12-26 <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Hi Wendy -- Thank you for the time you offered me to clarify if this offering was appropriate for me in 2026. At this time, it is not. May 2026 be a vital and remarkable year for you, and those you care about. </span><br><br>Warmly,<br>Matthew', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 12:08:11', '2026-01-12 12:08:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178499106', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130231002', 'Brian Groharing', NULL, 'Member called in and was confused because he had gotten a letter from Planstin that he was no longer covered.  Member had no information however said that it was for a Cardiac issue.  I told the member that 1. he no longer had Planstin now ARM &amp; that the bill had been submitted to the wrong place.  I then explained that anything that is not Preventative gets processed on the Medical Cost Sharing side and is subject to the $5000 IUA prior to anything being  shared.  I went through the cash paying scenario and how to present &amp; the gathering of bills to upload when opening a need.  He understood.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2026-01-12 12:08:09', '2026-01-12 12:08:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178551069', 'Matthew Hogan', NULL, '1-12-26 Hi Wendy, thank you for the well thought out email -- I can answer your two primary questions now.<br><br>1. I am self employed.<br>2. I am registered as a Florida resident, currently in Boulder<br>3. In business, I''m in a change phase, meaning I am not able to offer predicted income.<br><br>4. I don''t have any diagnosed conditions, based on my understanding of what diagnosis is.<br><br>As it sounds, it sounds like it would not be helpful to me to sign up -- given the current circumstances and understanding of what is offered<br><br>Be well,<br>Matt<br>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 12:07:40', '2026-01-12 12:07:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178554032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176543001', 'Stacy Hudson', '1/12/2026', 'RX Request x2 Ibandronate and Minoxidil. RC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-12 12:07:11', '2026-01-12 12:07:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178551069', 'Matthew Hogan', NULL, '1-12-26 Hi Wendy -- thank you for your willingness to receive an emailed question pertaining to the available coverage, that deadlines on January 15th -- for Feb 1 start.<br><br>Currently -- much of my care is restorative and preventative across a range of modalities, supplements and practitioners.<br><br>Current Care being received<br><br>Working with a MD in Boulder<br>- His hourly rate (I see him right now, about once a quarter) is $582<br>- He has suggested multiple supplements to support both restoration and prevention -- ~450 a month<br>- I have pending order for biochemical testing to be completed; testosterone, DHEA levels, and a few more bio-markers -- ~1500 pending investment<br><br>On an ongoing basis<br><br>- I am working with a Dr. of Chinese medicine, who partners with the MD mentioned above. Through herbs and acupuncture, she is supporting preventative and restorative care -- this $135 a session, 2-3 x a month<br><br>- I receive deep tissue and energetic massage 1x a month - 160 monthly<br><br>- I receive cranio-sacral every 3 weeks, working to restore functioning to brain-stem from years of physical stress - $245 every 3 weeks<br><br>- As directed by the above MD, I have a breathwork session once a month -- $100 <br><br>- I have a fitness membership at a local sauna where they blend suana + iso-metric workouts to support detoxing the system and building strength<br><br><b>Given the above care I am receiving, and the potential for it to increase, or decrease -- how would the available options for 2026 support me with these expenses, and continuing to receive the quality care that is oriented towards a progressive expression of optimal health? </b><br><br>Warmly,<br>Matthew', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 12:07:07', '2026-01-12 12:07:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178497455', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000177100004', 'Loren DeRiemacker', 'Member Only $5000 IUA Care +', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2026-01-12 12:06:24', '2026-01-12 12:06:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178551044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103065002', 'Lisa Dannen', NULL, '1-12-25 I called David to let him know he has to cancel his Zion membership. They aren''t letting me do it for him. He believes he''s finally and successfully cancelled it on his end and will be receiving his refund for the extra month they billed him. He will double check to find has confirmation and appreciated my call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-12 11:54:57', '2026-01-12 11:54:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178554021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173244004', 'Michael Cook', '1/12/2026', 'RX Request x4. RC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-12 11:54:42', '2026-01-12 11:54:42'),
