  ('zcrm_1579374000178133041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165338131', 'Hannah Blatter', NULL, '1-2-26 Hey Wendy,<br><br>I’m on my fiancé’s medical insurance for 2026, so that should all be good to go. If anything changes during the year I’ll reach out to you for help then. Happy new year!<br><br>Hannah Blatter', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-02 17:14:41', '2026-01-02 17:14:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178133026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136256011', 'Brian Coffey', NULL, '1-2-26 Brian is guessing he''ll make $40K-$50K, so we put in $45K for 2026. He''s choosing between the Anthem Gold Essentials plan for about $254 or Premium HSA for $336/$1500. He just had some slightly off labs for cholesterol but not meds prescribed. He needs Feb. 1st effective date. He''ll review everything over the weekend and call me on Monday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-02 16:20:42', '2026-01-02 16:20:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178133014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178561001', 'Genevieve Choi', NULL, '1-2-26 William and Genevieve are most concerned about William''s meds, Mounjaro, Repatha and Jardiance. They all say NOT Specialty but ther are Tier 3 or 4. It looks like they would be Preferred or Non-Preferred meaning $50 or $200 per month. One son plays hockey and needs jaw surgery from getting hit. So, he will be best served on the C4 plan with William. If all family members join C4 it will be $3540.09. They are paying $2900 for Cobra right now which is ending Jan. 31st. We will likely put 2 kids or all kids onto Premium HSA. One can double up with ACA RMHP/UHC plan with William until he does his jaw surgery and all is well. They each go to different schools and we don''t know if all schools will accept the MCS/MEC or not. They will discuss all of the options and. We have our next appt on Monday, Jan. 12th at 4:00 pm. She wants William''s help but I let her know I can do the C4 part and talk her through the MCS app. Kids are Olivia 24, William S, 24 soon and Cedric 21.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2026-01-02 16:07:42', '2026-01-02 16:07:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178068173', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000172083002', 'Keith Phillips', '1/2/25', '<br>Julie called in requesting a quicker response to her emails regarding her husband’s colonoscopy. Upon further review and assistance, I noted that the procedure was billed as a <b>diagnostic colonoscopy</b>.<br>I explained to Julie that due to the nature of the procedure, it is no longer considered <b>preventive</b>. She was advised not to submit the claim to MPB Health as preventive, but instead to proceed as <b>self-pay</b> and open a <b>sharing request</b>.<br>Julie expressed frustration and stated that she believed the procedure should be preventive. I explained that once a <b>polyp is found and removed</b>, the procedure is no longer classified as preventive. I further clarified that providers will not code the procedure as preventive once clinical findings are addressed in the medical record.<br>I emphasized that this is <b>not an MPB Health policy decision</b>, but rather the standard application of <b>CPT coding guidelines</b>, where removal of a polyp converts the service from preventive to routine/diagnostic care. AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:58:19', '2026-01-02 14:58:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120189', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155413001', 'Rebecca Jackson', NULL, '1/2/26<br>Answered her questions about what happens when they turn 65. Let them know they have to go to medicare and sent the cancel form just in case so they could have some peace of mind that they know it gets cancelled.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:50:51', '2026-01-02 14:50:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120170', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086318002', 'Zachary Weaver', NULL, '1/2/26<br>son got diagnosed with diabetes and wanted to know what the next steps were. I let him know to get any estimates and treatment plans he can to begin a share request. LEt him know we are here to walk him through the process if he needs<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:46:49', '2026-01-02 14:46:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178068168', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173394002', 'Stephen Prince', NULL, '1/2/25<br>Stephen called because he needed to kow what netwrok we use AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:40:45', '2026-01-02 14:40:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120165', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124631253', 'Ilysa Keeley', NULL, '1/2/26<br>reached out through email to see what to do with some preventative bills. I gave her instructions and the info on what to do with them in the future and what to do with the ones she has<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:38:55', '2026-01-02 14:38:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120160', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000177399002', 'Wendy Chou', NULL, '1/2/26<br>reached out to see how to cancel. i sent her the form in email<br>aJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:38:04', '2026-01-02 14:38:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120155', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012429101', 'Karyn Burke Whitcomb', NULL, '1/2/26<br>answered her email about login issues and helped walk her through what she needed to do<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:37:10', '2026-01-02 14:37:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120150', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163416002', 'Mefford Williams', NULL, '1/2/26<br>bill submission assistance, Mefford reached out to see what to do about some bills. I let him know where to send them and forwarded them then gave him the info on what to do with the bills in the future.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:36:31', '2026-01-02 14:36:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120142', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145730001', 'Lenissa Byrne', NULL, '1/2/26<br>spoke to lenissa about what would be covered for a medical transport back to the country. her daughter broke her back and needs special transport. we called zion together and they could not say 100% but they did not believe that would be covered and would likely be out of pocket<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:35:20', '2026-01-02 14:35:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120137', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113526002', 'Laurie Linn', NULL, '1/2/26<br>laurie called a couple times having troubles hooking up with the dr on telehealth. It looks like they finally linked up because she has not called back now to get them to connect<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:34:04', '2026-01-02 14:34:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120132', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088337002', 'Teresa Mullaney', NULL, '1/2/26 <br>Theresa reached out on sales IQ to find out how to add her spouse and what it would cost to upgrade. I gave her the numbers and the form so she could submit that for the upgrade<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:32:12', '2026-01-02 14:32:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000178120127', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176443017', 'Caroline Kinderthain', NULL, '1/2/26<br>telehealth login issues. I spoke to IT and we found out they will be delayed for all new members for another 24 hours until they can access the telehealth. let them know to reach ut if they still have trouble accessing telehealth after 24 hours.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2026-01-02 14:29:37', '2026-01-02 14:29:37'),
