  ('zcrm_1579374000177552013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154678123', 'Kevin Falardo', NULL, '12-23-25 Hi Wendy,<br>We were not happy with the insurance we had, and want a new plan, preferrably NOT Rocky Mountain Health Plans. It was a bad experience, and their company constantly dropped hte ball with coverage. It was such a pain.<br><br>But the biggest part of this is needing to add an employee to my insurance plan. Not under us, but as her own through my company. Is that something you can quote?<br><br>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-23 16:57:22', '2025-12-23 16:57:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000177552008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000167357006', 'Deborah Pope', NULL, '12-23-25 I sent this to Estella Wolff -  My client Deborah Pope continues to call RMHP/UHC to set up her payment starting about 10 business days past her enrollment date of Nov. 17th.  When she calls in they they can''t find her plan.  It''s clearly showing up on Connect for Health CO as the RMHP Valley Bronze Copay Focus ($0 Virtual Urgent Care, No Referrals). Her cost is $2.69.  She''s attempted to resolve the problem on Dec. 3rd and again on Dec. 5th, and none of the Customer Service Reps have been able to help her. More recently, she started tracking her calls per the below Ref. #''s. She started tracking her calls once it was clear nobody was finding her in the system or able to help her. <br><br>Deb Spoke with Rage on Dec. 12th with Ref # - SR54156365. After he talked with his Supervisor, they finally found her application in the queue but incomplete with the Bronze plan.  He mentioned she would owe the $2.69 premium once it was completed. He said her account from 2025 is set up on auto pay and it should roll over into 2026. But since she''s gotten the run around so many times, she called back again today to make sure all was well. <br> <br>Today she spoke with Colleen with Ref #INT47716308 who once again didn''t see her plan in the system and saw some random silver plan that she did not choose. Colleen was not able to confirm her auto-pay was good to go for the correct plan for 2026.<br><br>She even paid her last payment for her December plan of $6.96 twice on Dec. 2nd from two different bank accounts. One was through auto draft and the other was manual because she was trying so hard to make sure her plan for 2026 was set up and ready to go. However, she now has an overpayment and no proof that her account is ready to go moving forward for the $2.69 for January of 2026.<br><br>First and foremost, can you verify that her account will remain active and it will still deduct from her currently set up auto-pay around the 1st of the month. Secondly, how will she gain the refund of the double payment?', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-23 16:55:02', '2025-12-23 16:55:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000177552001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112994002', 'Carol VerMeer', NULL, '12-23-25 Carol called bc she has a colonoscopy scheduled for early Jan. and needs her new MEC card with the network and billing info. I recommended she calls the MPB Concierge Team and request her digital card to proceed. She will do that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-23 16:07:38', '2025-12-23 16:07:38'),
