  ('zcrm_1579374000176844012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176707012', 'Heather Boeke', 'Member Only $1250 IUA Secure HSA', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-12-18 06:22:16', '2025-12-18 06:22:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176844001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176735004', 'James Brown', 'Member Only $5000 IUA Care +', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-12-18 06:11:38', '2025-12-18 06:11:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176741132', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176740001', 'Loyal George', NULL, '12-17-25 <br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Hi Wendy,</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">1.</span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i> Regarding the pre-existing conditions. I have been diagnosed with Osteoporosis in the last two years. It''s been downgraded to osteopenia as of June of 2025. So I understand that this is considered a preexisting condition and any future treatment would not be covered. If I were to break a bone skiing would this be covered? </i></span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i>2. I had a colonoscopy within the last 2 years and had a couple of polyps removed. Is this a preexisting condition that would exclude me for any colon issues or cancer in the future? </i></span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i>Do you have answers about these nuances. I already shared what''s written in the Sharing Guidelines. So, they''ve read that for both questions and are trying to nail it down even further.</i></span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">For question #1:   A quick search:</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Where a pre-membership condition leads to a medical need is problematic.  </span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">A symptom of Osteopenia is weak bones .   If a new medical need that links back to the pre-existing condition, it''s likely it will not be eligible for sharing in the first year.  </span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">For question#2:  Same I think - depends on what''s in the medical records.  If there is a new medical need that is related to the polyp removal, its likely ineligible for sharing.  </span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">If it were me, I''d rather take the risk on the first one, probably not the second.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Hope this helps.</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">All good things,</span><br><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Rachelle</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-17 17:14:39', '2025-12-17 17:14:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176741127', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447059', 'Florie Glusman', NULL, '12-17-25 Florie completed the Change form to upgrade to Secure HSA from Care+.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-17 17:00:04', '2025-12-17 17:00:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176741116', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176792004', 'Jennifer Spinelli', NULL, '12-17-25 Jenn is 54 and husband is 46. They are both self-employed. They live in Avon, CO and were referred by Casey Richter. They are most interested in help with acute care for accidents. They are already paying cash for much of what they need such as going to a functional medicine dr. Her husband takes mental health meds. They had UHC for $1500 and $8K ded and not a similar plan is going to $1800 this year. They somehow have access to an Aetna plan. Her husband takes mental health meds and she has an inhaler for asthma. No other pre-x or tobacco. She chose Premium HSA and I explained possible balance billing in Avon for wellness. She understands. They are all set to go and happy to save $1000+ per month!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-17 15:05:32', '2025-12-17 15:14:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176741091', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163360057', 'Deborah Ares', NULL, '12-17-25 I''m talking with Maura from C4 to change Deb''s start date to Jan. 1st, 2026. I''m on hold while Maura is creating the escalation to do so. She submitted the escalation for the Jan. 1st start date. The Ref# is 543872-S2D9K9. They don''t have a time frame to share for when it will be done. If she needs to use the plan before the change is complete, she will just have to submit the information after the fact. Maura added a note to include me on the email communication when the new plan is set to go for Jan. 1st. All set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-17 14:59:46', '2025-12-17 15:10:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000176721066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000159899009', 'Michelle Ellis', NULL, '12/17/25<br>Sent email to follow up on sharing request AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-17 14:58:31', '2025-12-17 14:58:31'),
