  ('zcrm_1579374000176741001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176740001', 'Loyal George', NULL, '12-17-25 Berkeley (Loyal) and Julie have questions about:<br><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">1. Regarding the pre-existing conditions. I have been diagnosed with Osteoporosis in the last two years. It''s been downgraded to osteopenia as of June of 2025. So I understand that this is considered a preexisting condition and any future treatment would not be covered. If I were to break a bone skiing would this be covered? </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">2. I had a colonoscopy within the last 2 years and had a couple of polyps removed. Is this a preexisting condition that would exclude me for any colon issues or cancer in the future? </span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Do you have answers about these nuances. I already shared what''s written in the Sharing Guidelines. So, they''ve read that for both questions and are trying to nail it down even further.</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">I''m waiting for a little further clarification. If bad Julie can move to ACA via Cobra or LX.</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-17 09:35:44', '2025-12-17 09:35:44'),
