  ('zcrm_1579374000175747393', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175820002', 'Michael Carpenter', NULL, '12-9-25 <span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"> He signed up on his own today.  He''s all set! His wife and daughter are staying on their own path for now.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 00:08:16', '2025-12-10 00:08:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747388', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175820002', 'Michael Carpenter', NULL, '11-20-25 Wendy,<br><br>Thank you so much for the quick response.  I''ve watched your 9-minute video, explored your website, and also watched the interview with Cory Nickerson of 8Z.  <br><br>I agree with you that the Premium Care membership with an IUA of $1,500 and a monthly contribution amount of $267/month makes good sense for me starting Jan 1, 2026.  I understand there''s also a $125 initiation fee, which is fine.  Sign me up!  I''m ready to enroll, assuming I can cancel my membership in March 2026, right?<br><br>As for my wife (who is 59 years old) and her 23-year old daughter:  Neither have health issues that preclude them from using MPB Health.  My wife''s hesitancy is due to our frustrating experience with Redirect Health, which we used for a couple of years.  We found the slow pre-approvals, the uploading of invoices and the struggle to receive reimbursements to be maddening.  I''m sure your service is much, much better.  But my wife has recently enjoyed the traditional Anthem coverage we''ve had the past year.  She still hasn''t decided, though, so I''ll keep telling her about all her options.<br><span><br></span> I''ll be sure to refer you to anyone in need of this type of health cost sharing.<br><br>I look forward to getting enrolled.<br><br>Mike Carpenter<br>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 00:07:18', '2025-12-10 00:07:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747378', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088254024', 'Juana Rincon Barrios', NULL, '12-9-25 <br><p style="">December 9, 2025 at 6:15 PM</p><p style=""><span><br></span></p><p style="">Dear <span style=" margin-inline-start:20px;">Wendy Scipione</span>,</p><p style="">Juana Rincon Barrios has asked that you no longer work on his or her behalf to purchase insurance through Connect for Health Colorado®.</p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-10 00:01:26', '2025-12-10 00:01:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747373', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178071067', 'Jessica Zalkin', NULL, '12-9-25 Jessica was referred to me by Cory Nickerson. She''s a realtor like Cory. No pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. Dealing with peri-menopause and wants to go to a local DPC call Miss Medicine if they have openings. Dr. is Lindsay Cassidy. She''s wanting Premium Care $299/$1000 and then pair with DPC. She knows of the $125/$25 and wants Jan. 1st. She will let me know as soon as she''s able to reach the DPC to decide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 23:57:03', '2025-12-09 23:57:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747363', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000137203027', 'Mary Campbell', NULL, '12-9-25 Left vm for Mary. Need to try again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 23:52:12', '2025-12-09 23:52:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747355', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000172130002', 'Tami Schweitzer', NULL, '12-9-25 Tami wants to review C4 plans for them because Ivan is nervous MCS won''t pay out. The plans are $1700+ for terrible options. It looks like $1900 is where you finally get some benefits. I suggested she has him move to C4 and she stays put. She likes that idea. He also might change his mind once he sees the cost and lack of benefits. She knows the deadline. I sent her a sample set of plans to review. They might want access to UC Health and Select Health is best. Otherwise Cigna is best.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 23:46:51', '2025-12-09 23:47:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747275', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175937004', 'Douglas Haslinger', NULL, '12-9-25 UPDATE - "''m currently under treatment for obesity which I realize will not be covered under the Health Share as a pre-existing condition (it''s not covered under ACA either) however; are complications that may be linked to obesity, such as cardiac workups, sleep apnea, or gallbladder disease also capped at 3000 or is it treated separately?  If I had a heart attack in the first 12 months, how much is realistically shareable given that I have treated hypertension and obesity?<br><br>I''m considering if I should, myself, stay on an ACA plan (depending on the answers you have for me above). If I were to do that, could my husband and children still get the healthshare (my husband has his own business also with an EIN). If so, what would the cost per month be for him + our three kids.<br><br>Thanks for the additional information!"<br><span><br></span>Letting her know it''s safest to keep her on ACA and her husband and kids can join MCS.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 21:15:46', '2025-12-09 21:15:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747270', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005011193', 'Andre Mpitsos', NULL, '12-9-25 Andre asked about HAB and prefers to keep Care+ and possibly upgrade to Secure HSA in the first few months of the year when he can focus on it and might need wellness. His dr. accepts the PHCS network. He''ll also call to see what he''d charge as self-pay to see if that makes sense instead. He was happy for my call and we''ll talk when he''s ready to make changes. He owns his own biz as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 18:15:22', '2025-12-09 18:15:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747260', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129625123', 'Casey Zahorik', NULL, '12-9-25 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Casey Zahorik</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Anthem Silver Pathway Essentials 5000 $0 Select Drugs</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$100</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$950</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>$18.71 /month </b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">after $478.99 financial help</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Exchange policy number:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 7844960003</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Coverage dates:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Last updated:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 12/09/25</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 16:52:21', '2025-12-09 16:52:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747255', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129625123', 'Casey Zahorik', NULL, '12-9-25 Case is in the hospital right now bc of a nasal surgery problem. He alsmost went septic! He was totally fine with talking with Kim and I about his ins. They don''t want Medicaid bc they need his Dr. Nathan Roesner. He''s showing up in the Anthem Essentials Pathway network. Case will call and double check. We chose a Gold Anthem plan for 2026 and put his income est. at $23K. He can''t work for a while. He''s hoping to get a job in later 2026 with benefits if possible.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 16:52:13', '2025-12-09 16:52:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747245', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000689078', 'Kim Gangwish Zahorik', NULL, '12-9-25 Kim called BCH to see if Dr. Hansen is in the Anthem network and Anthem won''t accept any gyn without the ob part. They have to offer ob and they don''t. So, the cash price for a visit is $110 and the labs are covered with Anthem since Anthem is covered by BCH. So, she will save $100+ per month with this Anthem Gold plan vs the Cigna Connect Bronze $0. It makes sense for her to choose Anthem. She''s all set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 16:48:22', '2025-12-09 16:48:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747235', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000689078', 'Kim Gangwish Zahorik', NULL, '12-9-25 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Kimberly Gangwish Zahorik</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Anthem Colorado Option Gold Pathway Essentials Std</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$2,050</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$9,600</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color: