  ('zcrm_1579374000175747145', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109357046', 'Nicole Lubeck', NULL, 'I received VM from this member wanting to change her membership to the Care + eff 1/1/26.  I sent Change link and left member a VM to fill out.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-12-09 11:30:03', '2025-12-09 11:30:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175747140', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134180005', 'Lisa Ben-Zeev', NULL, '12-9-25 Lisa hates RMHP bc they billed her 5 ways for 1 visit. She wound up paying $1600 for her colonoscopy. But, now she''s seeing with the current options she may pay up to $2050 ded and then 30% co-ins. So, that''s not any better. I started showing her the tools for cash pay. After much go around and frustration with C4 plans I explained Premium Care. She''s not self-employed. She lives off investment income and that will be $61K for 2026 according to her accountant.  The Anthem CO Option  Gold Essentials plan will be $387.97 for her in 2026 but she''s upset by the coins for the things she might need. She has ulcerative colitis and takes meds for that. She does take covid shot and knows she would have to cash pay for that. I sent her the video to watch for Premium Care $299/$1000, $125/$25. I told her she has to be at peace with her pre-x and make sure to talk to her Dr. and review her records if she''s nervous. I don''t know what can become of that. She''s super ffrustrated with our healthcare system. She thought the APTC''s were gone but she''s getting about $654 + $80 or so towards C4 plans.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-09 11:24:57', '2025-12-09 11:24:57'),
