  ('zcrm_1579374000175744005', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173862021', 'Bruce Gauker', NULL, 'Member submitted Dependent Over 18 Form. I will process. Information in both CRM &amp; e123 were already added.', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-12-09 06:23:43', '2025-12-09 06:26:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646194', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176128017', 'Kelly Locke', NULL, '12-8-25 Kelly (Male) is 60 and his wife Karen is around 60 as well. They were referred by Martha Rybak. Karen is losing their ins through her employer for Jan. 1st, 2026. They will both be self-employed. They live in Basalt, CO. Kelly is taking a statin for high cholesterol. 7 years ago he had a heart arythmia which was treated with ablation. He hasn''t had any problems since. He also had a colon polyp 10 years ago and no problems since. He doesn''t need another colonoscopy for another 3-5 years. They had an HSA a long time ago. Yes, they do their wellness visits. We discussed Premium HSA or Secure HSA. Oh he also had glaucoma which was removed and no problem since. I think this is the only thing that was within the pre-x time frame, I think within 1 year or so. They spend a bunch of time in AK as well as CO. He will share with Karen and is likely to choose one of these options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 23:22:27', '2025-12-10 23:25:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646179', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175646163', 'Rivers Rothkamp', NULL, '12-8-23 Angie is helping her 20 year old daughter, River get ins. DOB 2/3/2005 in 80129, Douglas County. She''s a student and has paid her own way through school. Angie started the conversation with $23K and then was waivering between $30K-$50K and wants to know every variation of plan choices. She learned a lot and will play with the numbers on her own and talk with River. River has hip dysplasia and needs a very specific surgery who very few Drs. able good at. They want Dr Phillipon with Steadman''s clinic. The only plans who include him are the Anthem Pathway plans. She''s calling around to find out if Vail Health and Vail Surgery Center will accept it. Nobody will give her straight answers. She will press on and keep me posted. Rivers is a student and work for a turf/sod company. The surgery will dictate how much time she takes off from work and has to manage school as well. She''s a very hard worker though.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 23:11:23', '2025-12-08 23:11:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646154', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155265018', 'Brian Loften', NULL, '12-8-25 Spoke with Brian about HAB and what included and Premium Care and what''s included. I encouraged him to make use of his HAB membership while he can.  He may try to get in his dental cleaning, vision screening, submit for a new gym membership, etc. He will refresh his mind on the rest of the information I sent to him.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 20:32:40', '2025-12-08 20:32:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646149', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174894039', 'James Lerner', NULL, '12-8-25 James got approved for Medicaid per his mom via Cari. They asked me to cancel his plan for 2026 which I did. He should be all set moving forward with Medicaid for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 18:14:47', '2025-12-08 18:14:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646131', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779247', 'Todd Wells', NULL, '12-8-25 Todd is still active in cycling and sometimes wins prize money and Secure HSA won''t share in any costs related to his cycling if he gets injured bc he''s getting paid on occasion. He''s moving to Premium HSA and he''s self-employed. This will protect him while cycling. He doesn''t have any pre-x and neither does in son Cooper. He''s moving him as well bc it''s more affordable. Meghan needs to stay with Secure HSA bc she has a hip issue going on right now that would be pre-x. She has her own company. He thinks she uses her SS# and doesn''t have an EIN. She splits her time with W2 and 1099 but will keep her business intact either way. He''s choosing $1500/$615 Premium HSA EC. Then Meghan will do Secure HSA $1250/$448. I waived the $100 since they are already members with MPB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 16:26:53', '2025-12-08 16:36:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175646126', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155322082', 'Valerie Reynolds', NULL, '12-8-25 Keith is aging into Medicare. Valerie chose the RMHP Gold. It''s less than $2 her cost and the best plan for the price. She''s all set. She works a seasonal job and ins will start April of 2026. So, she just needs this for 3 months.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-08 15:30:15', '2025-12-08 15:30:15'),
