  ('zcrm_1579374000175149035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174097018', 'Stephanie Markham', '12/3/25', 'Stephanie wanted to know how to access her digital card in the app  AC<br><span><br></span>', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-03 21:13:06', '2025-12-03 21:13:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187138', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162057106', 'Deland Craven', NULL, '12-3-25 Deland''s request to me:<br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Wendy,</span><br><br>Hope you’re doing well and your Thanksgiving was great. Here’s where things stand…<br><br>- I think I finished my CIGNA open enrollment by basically approving the changes to my current plans… ya know… pay more get less.<br>- I have a full time job that does not provide benefits and the pay is going to change my estimated income. It’s hourly so it’s very variable.<br>- I “think” my income for 2026 will be around $60K. I had estimated $50K for 2025 and should be under that.<br>- Ideally I’d like to switch from CIGNA dental to Delta Dental if possible but would be fine to just keep whatever I approved with my open enrollment.<br>- It seems like I have some open switches to close to update to my “I have a job and am macing a bit more money”.<br><br>Any help is appreciated. I tried to go on the Colorado site last week but it keep erroring out.<br><br>Cheers!<br>Deland<br><span><br></span>My response to her:<br>Hi Deland,<br><br>Here''s what your account shows for 2026 . I updated your income to $60K. I removed the self-employment job. You had $250 showing for alimony/spousal payment which is $3K annually. That brings your income to $57K for 2026. Is that what you want? If so, see below for the costs and the plans you chose. Dental auto renewed already. <br><br><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Health</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Deland Craven</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(36, 126, 180);"><b>1-800-244-6224</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Cigna Connect Flex Gold 1200 Rx Copay</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">Gold/EPO</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>$1,264.34</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>$684.61</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Dental</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Deland Craven</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(36, 126, 180);"><b>1-800-244-6224</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>Cigna Dental Family + Pediatric</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">Low/PPO</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>$32.96</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);"><b>$0</b></span></p><br>Let me know if this is accurate and good to go!<br><br>Cheers,', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 20:35:13', '2025-12-03 20:35:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187123', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130286061', 'David Naber', NULL, '12-3-25 Dave asked me to renew their current plan which I did. I sent them the proof via email. Their cost will be less than last year!  They are all set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 20:17:39', '2025-12-03 20:17:39'),
