  ('zcrm_1579374000175187108', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162402001', 'Ariel Tidwell', NULL, '12-3-25 It looks like Ariel removed my message from her text. Her vm is full. So, it seems that she doesn''t want to be reached. I also sent an email. There''s not much more I can do.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 20:15:31', '2025-12-03 20:15:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010282133', 'Susan Atchison', NULL, '12-3-25 Left vm to complete her enrollment for Premium Care. Enrolling now EF for Jan. 1st. I waived the $100 fee for her as a previous member. All set for 2026!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 16:05:03', '2025-12-03 20:18:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156186015', 'Noah Burleson', NULL, '12-3-25 Noah was considering lower his IUA with their saving of $107 per month. But, with the new pricing it''s a bigger price difference for the $1250 IUA which would be $816 instead of $642. They''ll keep the $642 for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 15:57:28', '2025-12-03 15:57:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012010011', 'Elizabeth Wood', NULL, '12-3-25 Elizabeth is trying to remember how she access Eloquis very affordably before and I think it''s Drexi through HAB due to the name she came close to being Drexi. I told her to contact the Concierge if that''s not helpful.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 15:47:29', '2025-12-03 15:47:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187080', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175165052', 'Christopher Bramley', NULL, '12-3-25 All the plans were close in what might be best. We finally narrowed it down to Premium Care for the price in his age group as he turns 50 next year. He doesn''t care about the wellness benefits and will pay for his 1 visit and labs. Chose $1000/$299 $125/$25 EO Jan. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 15:19:17', '2025-12-03 15:19:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175187153', 'Amy Anderson', NULL, '12-3-25 No answer. Trying again now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 14:40:22', '2025-12-03 14:40:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010282133', 'Susan Atchison', NULL, '<span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">12-3-25 Susan was facing facing $3300 ACA plan for the family.  She will choose Premium Care. She''s already done her mammo and colonoscopy. Brad will wait until he hits Medicare. Kids are fine for wellness. So, Premium Care is better priced than Care+ and gives more benefits. She will make her way home and we will get the family enrolled $1000/$877 or $1500/$777. Waive $100 since member previously. They are both self-employed.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 14:38:09', '2025-12-03 14:38:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175146189', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120893013', 'Ashley Sargent', NULL, '12/3/25<br>Spoke with Ashley and realized she could send in another chance at getting reimbursed for Colo bill since they called it diagnostic. I let her know she can start a share request pay her IUA then she should be able to get the rest of the bill shared on to help knock down the large bill<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-03 14:36:25', '2025-12-03 14:36:55'),
