  ('zcrm_1579374000175146106', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124104002', 'Sherwin Miguel', NULL, '12/3/25<br>Sent sherwin a f/u to let him know due to HIPPA he needs to help us be able to speak to MSEAP if he needs us to, Let him know that he can reach out to them at the number i gave him to see what the issue is with his counselor. If he has any trouble or needs any guidance i let him know to reach out for us to be able to help him.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-03 12:57:51', '2025-12-04 11:11:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175146099', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110308002', 'Robert Golden', NULL, '12/3/25<br>Spoke to robert about his IUA and the upcoming price increase. Let him know how he would be affected. Also explained the referral process because he has a freind who might be signing up.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-03 12:51:05', '2025-12-03 12:51:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163494009', 'Katherine Totten', NULL, '12-2-25 Kate will keep Premium Care since she''s not employed or working right now. She may do some 1099 work. She can upgrade at that time if she wants. She will let HAB lapse and leave that alone. She''s interested in possible dietician work with Teresa and labs under the $4500 category. She''s in school right now with Cornell to get some type of professional certificate. She''s used her dental for $250 and will work on doing the vision part for $250 as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 12:49:56', '2025-12-03 12:49:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175143178', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082410002', 'Nicholas Burdick', NULL, '12/3/25 - Spoke with member regarding laboratory orders for Jonah. Letter was e-mailed with total cost &amp; directions for <br>submitting. SW', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-03 12:37:27', '2025-12-03 12:37:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060125007', 'Michael Remacle', NULL, '12-3-25 Michael is making progress with the bills for Kyle. He''s working with Rachel on the Determination Team for the finl $9K in LabCorp bills. There was confusion in the communications about what was outstanding and accepted per Dr. Melamed''s bills and Lab Corps bills. Dr. Melamed  with Veros had a $75 bill vs the $9K in Lab Corp. Zion gave him a month to dispute the Veros bill which he thought only pertained to $75. But, they were referring to the Lab Corp bill even though in the past they always referred to those bills specifically as Lab Corp. So, he''s going to show proof about that failed communication and see if they''ll share the rest of the $9K and stay the course. Michael is in much better spirits about all of it. They finally determined that Kyle had a walking pneumonia! Dr. Melamed has given him a course of antibiotics and is doing much better finally! It was affecting him neurologically. But, he''s now going to CU!!  Kyle also may qualify for Medicaid still. We resubmitted the application since it forced me down that path to be able to apply for 2026 for Hilary on C4.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 12:33:24', '2025-12-03 12:33:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175187040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062699001', 'Hilary Remacle', NULL, '12-3-25 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">hilary remacle</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Cigna Connect HSA Bronze 6500</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">30% (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$6,500</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$8,300</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">30% (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">30% (after deductible)</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:fle