  ('zcrm_1579374000175187006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175202002', 'Gregory Hubachek', NULL, '12-3-25 We are talking again today to continue the conversation. Greg is fully retired and no side income. He''s 62 and lives in NV. His best option will be Premium Care for the wellness. He takes meds for high blood pressure, cholesterol and heart disease. I made it abundantly clear that if he has anything go wrong with his heart or has heart attack that will be his cost 100% in year one. He said he''s not planning to have a heart attack. He''s comfortable with the risk. He even wanted the highest IUA until I showed him and explained the math. Then he recognized it makes more sense to choose the lower IUAs. He chose $1500/$267 Premium Care Jan. 1st 2026 EO.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-03 09:48:42', '2025-12-03 10:21:46'),
