  ('zcrm_1579374000175053207', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069438001', 'Beth Blacker', NULL, '12-2-25 Beth''s income is at $51,740 from last year. We''ll leave it alone.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 21:44:59', '2025-12-02 21:44:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053202', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176443053', 'Lisa LeVerrier', NULL, '12-1-25 Lisa is 62 and husband will be 64 in April. They were referred by Willow Aureala and live in Boca Raton, FL 33432. Her husband has ADHD and excema or some derm condition. They both have hypothyroid. Their daughter had some surgery this past year and may stay on trad ins until everything is 100% good. I sent her the video. She and her husband are both self-employed and both have EINs.They do a little domestic travel and might go intl this coming year. We discussed Secure HSA MS $1250/$774 or $2500/$646. Lisa had a colonoscopy and it was all clear. She take HRT, does her pap, mammo and labs.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 21:33:14', '2025-12-02 21:33:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053189', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175165052', 'Christopher Bramley', NULL, '12-2-25 Chris is 49 and turning 50 on July 20th 2026. He came to me via Alicia Thompson. He''s currently on the marketplace but he is in HA in the winter and CO in the summer. He''s self-employed, healthy, no meds, no tobacco and yes for wellness 1x per year. He''s alredy done his colonoscopy and doesn''t need one again for a long. We talked about all 4 memberships bc he''s on the cusp of turning 50, so there''s no clear membership that''s best. He might not need to pay the extra monthly for ACA wellness screenings. He was starting to enroll in Secure HSA for the alternative care and HSA compliance but then it was more expensive than he realized with so many options I gave to him. So, he needs to review it all and compare and contrast first. He also will benefit from the supplement discounts. He''s active with sports, yoga and likes massage, chiro, alertnative care, etc. He likes to get his PSA checked for prostate issues due to his dad having unusual PSA. But, he had to pay out of pocket for that already since ins didn''t cover it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 21:03:50', '2025-12-02 21:03:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053143', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175187153', 'Amy Anderson', NULL, '12-2-25 Amy lives in Louisville and Cobra just ended. She needs Jan. 1st start date. She''s 57. She had a policy with Cigna Open Access PPO. She wants to be able to choose her doctors and keep the ded down. She''s healthy. She takes HRT and a thyroid med. Sounds like a good fit for MCS. She''s going to watch the video before we talk tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 20:23:01', '2025-12-02 20:23:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053133', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078963251', 'Denise Schulz', NULL, '12-2-25 Denise chose a plan under pressure of the Dec. 1st deadline. She thought the PCP visits were $0 under the new plan. However, that''s after the $10,600 ded and mop that it''s $0. So, she''s prefer to pay $50 more per month to have co-pays for Dr. visits and other items. She needs to update her address also to a new zip code of 80118. We''ll change the zip and then change the plan back to the <span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>RMHP Colorado Doctors Plan Bronze Value ($0 Virtual Urgent Care, No Referrals) at $231.43.</b></span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 20:04:36', '2025-12-02 20:04:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053125', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078963251', 'Denise Schulz', NULL, '12-2-25 <br> <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Denise Schulz</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>RMHP Colorado Doctors Plan Bronze Essential ($0 Virtual Urgent Care, No Referrals)</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$0 (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$10,600</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$10,600</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$0 (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$0 (after deductible)</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>$177.90 /month </b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">after $861.55 financial help</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Exchange policy number:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 1501038371</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Coverage dates:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;margin-inline-start:0.5rem;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Last updated:</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"> 12/01/25</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 19:18:41', '2025-12-02 19:22:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053120', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059893072', 'Elaine Roth', NULL, '12-2-25 Left vm with Jefferson to help him with a solution for Isabelle, his daughter for Jan. 2026.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 16:52:41', '2025-12-02 16:52:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053115', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109184005', 'Merryl Rothaus', NULL, '12-2-25 Merryl moved to Asheville, NC. She wants help with HAB and possibly ACA. But, if no subsidy then I can help her with other options. I left her a long vm.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 16:50:03', '2025-12-02 16:50:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174963059', 'Laura Waldman', NULL, '12-2-25 Laura''s dr. and RMHP are telling her that her plan expired. She now sees that she can make a payment to keep it active. She''s making her payment now. 1st try was declined and trying another method for $879.52. Once she pays it should be good. The payment went through. Everything shows as Active and in good standing on the C4 site. She will call RMHP if she has any further troubles.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 16:41:26', '2025-12-02 16:45:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175042024', 'Jolene Blair', NULL, '12-2-25 Jolene is 64. Her Cigna Connect CO Option Bronze plan is $700+ in 2025 and will go to $1107 for 2026. She thought it was going to $2300. I think she added her husband Jim by accident. He''s 68 and on Medicare. They live in Windsor, CO. She''s healthy, just takes a tiny 2.5 mg dose of high blood pressure med lisinopril and valocyclovir. No tobacco. Retired but has rental income and uses SS. Income will be about $138K, above APTC threshold. They chose Premium HSA to fund the HSA for 2026, $1000/$363. They are thrilled to save so much money and have much lower IUA. They also watched the video before we talked.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 15:56:36', '2025-12-02 15:56:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053092', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175113002', 'Carrie Kudrna', NULL, '12-2-25 Carrie 63 is choosing Care+. She doesn''t plan to do the wellness stuff until she hits Medicare. She did a mammo not too long ago and is not interested in the rest. She''s retired and also has some rental properties with an LLC if she needs to upgrade at any time. She losing Cobra. ACA was going to be $900-$1000. She has stuff from 2022 but that''s in the past before the 24 month pre-x. The most recent health stuff is gastro and constipation. She had some levels that were off but they''ve been checked and the doctors can''t find anything wrong. She had a cyst on her spine that is fine. I''m not sure when that was, possibly also around 2022.  She enrolled in Care+ and completed the rest on her own after some troubles.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 15:03:37', '2025-12-02 20:44:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175032056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153824002', 'Samuel Young', NULL, '12/2 answered Sun You''s email asking us to confirm her appt in Feb, 2026 with Andrea Milne. Informed her that that doctor  is currently in network but to check with the providers office on the day of the appointment to confirm. DM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-02 14:43:44', '2025-12-02 14:43:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175049126', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174681003', 'Diana Ball', NULL, '12/2/25<br>Sent Diana the quote for her labs via email AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-02 14:43:01', '2025-12-02 14:43:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175049113', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000166458002', 'Oscar Echeverri', NULL, '12/2/25<br>Called to follow up with him regarding his knee injury he has reached his IUA will make an email with instruction on how to open the zion portal AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-12-02 14:20:01', '2025-12-02 14:20:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000175053082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091330', 'Krista Rogers', NULL, '12-2-25 Krista is considering increasing her IUA from $1250 to $2500 for final 8 months before she moves to Medicare. She can do her wellness visits at that point. She''s already done all of her wellness stuff through HAB and is good to go for a while. Her income is not steady right now, so the $2500/$318 is appealing for Care+.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-02 14:15:04', '2025-12-02 14:15:04'),
