  ('zcrm_1579374000174963158', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129549019', 'Eva Nemcik', NULL, '12-1-25 <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">evanemcik36@gmail.com just purchased a plan from your link! You will earn commission once the member is active beyond the 30-day trial period.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 23:38:06', '2025-12-01 23:38:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963153', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000151764180', 'Michelle Ruyle', NULL, '12-1-25 She asked me to opt her out of auto renew. Sounds like she''s all set. But, I sent her the two lowest cost plans that are in alignment with what she''s paying this year. We''ll see if she responds.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 23:28:04', '2025-12-01 23:28:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963143', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152311057', 'Daniel Richardson', NULL, '12-1-25 1Dental - <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">richardson@rof.net just purchased a plan from your link! You will earn commission once the member is active beyond the 30-day trial period.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 23:12:33', '2025-12-01 23:12:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963138', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152311057', 'Daniel Richardson', NULL, '12-1-25 Dan chose to upgrade to Premium HSA since he''ll be losing HAB for Jan. 1st. He''s also adding 1Dental for dental and vision discounts.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 23:06:09', '2025-12-01 23:06:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963133', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174963099', 'Pamela Kalechovsky', NULL, '12-1-25 <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Hi Wendy, </span><br><br>Thank you so much for all your time and information. I truly appreciate it and think this is a wonderful option for healthcare. <br><br>I just found out that I am able to be on my partner''s insurance, so I will be moving forward with healthcare through his plan.  Had that not worked out, I was absolutely going to enroll through you.  <br><br>If you don''t mind, I will hang on to your info for the future or pass it on to anyone who is interested. <br><br>Thank you again for all your time, thorough explanations, knowledge, and guidance. You are truly a gem &amp; I am most appreciative! <br><br>Hope you have a beautiful holiday season! <br><br>Best,<br>Pam', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 22:57:58', '2025-12-01 22:57:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144228001', 'Cynthia Franceus', NULL, '12-1-25 She''s looking at the Kaiser CO Silver Option for only $7.49. It will keep her costs down since they can''t afford the above plans.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 22:41:30', '2025-12-01 22:41:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144228001', 'Cynthia Franceus', NULL, '12-1-25 Cynthia and William are getting divorced but they are not yet. They are thinking about $32K income while together. She understands they can both make changes once they get divorced. For now they are deciding between their current Cigna <span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>Connect Colorado Option Silver for $306.55 or Anthem Colorado Option Silver Pathway Essentials Std for $156.45. The biggest difference is for her drugs Repatha 140MG/ML Sureclick and Trulicity. Anthem looks like they are both in lower tiers for lower pricing. So, Anthem may be the best and is half the price.  </b></span><br><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><br></span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 22:09:55', '2025-12-01 22:09:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174954035', 'Adrian Montemayor', NULL, '12-1-25 Adrian was referred to me by Sephra!  I thought it was by Aaron Montemayor. Adrian works for FAA and was stuck in all of the holiday travel craziness getting home from LA to FL. He''s 49 and his wife is 31. They are both super healthy. He just gets ear infections from doing water sports. He takes a blood pressure med and a med for gout. Otherwise he''s healthy as well. No tobacco. They live in FL, so Premium memberships are not an option. They plan to do their wellness screenings and Aaron also has some 1099 contract work and his own LLC. Secure HSA was the choice and it''s about 1/3 of the cost. He was going to have to pay about $1700 or something ridiculous for their ACA plan. He takes alopurinol and something else. He will contact the Concierge for pricing on the meds once he''s active. He''ll schedule his welcome call. He set up his ACH and he believes his current ins ins''t auto renewable. He''ll make sure so he doesn''t get charged again. He''s all set for a Jan 1st, 2026 start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 22:04:01', '2025-12-01 22:04:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163519006', 'Mary Steiner', NULL, '12-1-25 Helped her get a better plan than what she initially chose and for much less money. She''s happy. The RMHPMonument One Bronze Essentials gave her NO benefits for a higher cost. So, she chose the Select Health plan for $4.18 her cost instead with a $6900 Ded and co-pay for some stuff such a PCP, labs, urgent care etc.  All set for 2026 and knows to set up pmt and cancel current payment by Dec. 20th.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-12-01 18:25:25', '2025-12-01 18:25:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174963029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163519006', 'Mary Steiner', NULL, '12-1-25 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Peter Steiner, mary Steiner</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Select Health Monument Value Bronze $6900 Medical Deductible</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$13,800</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$21,200</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$90 (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="displ