  ('zcrm_1579374000174342027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174031002', 'Cheryl Roth', NULL, '11/24/25 - Responded to e-mail from member re: Dr. Rebecca Pestle . Will check again to determine if MD is in network. SW', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-24 07:17:44', '2025-11-24 07:17:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174307025', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174963099', 'Pamela Kalechovsky', NULL, '11-21-25 Pamela is 45 and she has a domestic partner who is 44. She might be allowed to join her partner''s employer plan. They are inquiring now. Pam says she''s healthy but does have "long covid" maybe. She had cancer in 2008 and her thyroid was removed. She''s had no problems ever since. She just has to take synthroid for the rest of her life since she has no thyroid. She has W2 employment and teaches yoga and other side jobs that are 1099. She needs a bi-lateral mammo every year for dense breasts. She takes some supplements and might benefit from the discounts. She wants to be able to go to Vanderbilt for care and that is showing in the PHCS network. She also needs a root canal. I sent her the dental discount plan to review. She''ll keep me posted.  Secure HSA will be best price and most comprehensive benefits. She took the J&amp;J and booster but is not a fan of regular flu shots. She loved her doctors in NY but doesn''t love who she''s seen so far. I thought she said NC but Nashville is in TN. So, I have something confused. Either way, she wants new doctors and is hoping for the same type of care she had in NY.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-22 14:08:24', '2025-11-22 14:10:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174307009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124369011', 'Rachel Weitz', NULL, '11-21-25 They expect to make about $125K for the 2 of them which is over the APTC level. They will have to pay full price. Once we looked at the plans and costs they started to do the math. Dan is seeing how brutal insurance will be as well. WIth the high cost of premiums, plus high ded and mop, he''s not sure if it benefits them to move to C4 or not. I showed him the esimator tool and he will run some numbers. They also got rejected from help with paying for Zoladex since they mentioned health sharing membership even though it''s not insurance. I recommended they try again since they do NOT have insurance and may qualify for help with the drugs. He will look into that. I think it was  Cigna that was the only one showing $600 co-pay for specialty drugs. The drug is tier 4. Anthem Pathway (not essentials) did NOT include Zoladex. I think Cigna and Anthem were the only two carriers that accept her cancer drs. So, that limited it to Cigna only. If it wasn''t Cigna then it was Select Health giving her access to UC Health as well. It looks like bc they didn''t follow the "Standard of Care" this might be why they are getting cut off by Zion. I''m not sure.  They tried some experimental options according to my notes from above.  She also needs Zometa which iasn''t showing up in the drug searches for either carrier. Letrazole is showing a $0 for 2.8 mg tablet. Dr. Katie Egan is in my notes for Dr.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-22 13:48:22', '2025-11-22 13:49:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174307001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044575094', 'Doug Klof', NULL, '11-21-25 <i>I have a client whose wife wants to join their membership. She learned 8 years ago that she has the BRCA2 gene. She''s been doing the recommended screenings since then. Nothing has ever shown up as any problem at all, for all 8 years. Is she clear of the pre-existing conditions clause, waiting period and tiered sharing?</i><br><br>Answer:<br><br><i>The screenings themselves would be pre-ex, but if something was diagnosed it would not be. As long as there are no medical records showing symptoms, diagnosis, treatment.</i>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-22 13:33:17', '2025-11-22 13:33:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174306001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155437001', 'Heather Klof', NULL, '11-21-25 See Doug''s account for more notes.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-22 12:57:16', '2025-11-22 12:57:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626120', 'Russell Finsterwald', NULL, '11-21-25 This is the response from Zion.  We need to move him or find accident ins.<br><span><br></span><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">I''m afraid that if a member is a professional athlete then medical expenses related to injuries sustained while training </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i>(practice)</i></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>will not be shareable</b></span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"> - irrespective of insurance coverage.   Please see:</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><a style="color:rgb(23, 78, 134);display:inline;" target="_blank" href="https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__zionhealthshare.org_how-2Dit-2Dworks_member-2Dguidelines_&amp;d=DwMFaQ&amp;c=euGZstcaTDllvimEN8b7jXrwqOf-v5A_CdpgnVfiiMM&amp;r=dVT6mh2rJEvNldIIymVnN6cN9mVnz23yakDKr-Yqv6Q&amp;m=pH3bqtmWqRS88b8utH4Ta9jmxfGFREwq67bXQNmyWSQf2m981j-OMXiGb2T_e3kv&amp;s=XVJk2qy9dRsRAXJXbUbSOxXHZ-266yuXxYRsh71ftBc&amp;e="><u>https://zionhealthshare.org/how-it-works/member-guidelines/</u></a></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">Zion HealthShare''s medical cost sharing community helps with unexpected medical needs is really not designed to share in those kinds of medical needs - they are sort of, well, </span><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><i>expected.</i></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></span></p><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">There are a variety of ways to access and pay for healthcare but, if the idea is to insure against that particular kind of risk, then the best solution is likely a traditional insurance plan.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 19:43:59', '2025-11-21 19:43:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178071246', 'Ann Inai', NULL, '11-21-25 She''s leaning towards Premium HSA for 2026 and $1000/$299 or $1500/$267. Let her know about the $125/$25. We will talk on Monday to enroll her and 12:30 while she''s in CA for a trip.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 16:56:03', '2025-11-21 16:56:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178071246', 'Ann Inai', NULL, '11-21-25 Ann is an acupuncturist with her own practice, self-employed. She''s 55 and lives in Denver, solo. She makes too much now to get an APTC. She''s currently paying about $400 and it includes dental and vision with an APTC for medical. 2026 will be $781 which she can''t afford. She really just wants the mammogram and ultrasound for dense breasts, colonoscopy every 5 years, pap screenings etc. She doesn''t take any meds, no tobacco and is healthy. She also found a UHC plan called Select Plus for $570 ish per month but it doesn''t include the wellness screenings. I described Premium HSA and Secure HSA. I found Dr. Thomas Li showing up in the PHCS network but not Dr. McAleese or Alison Herman. She had to hop off to remove the needles from her patient and will call me back.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 16:40:59', '2025-11-21 16:40:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063253037', 'Bobbi Georgeton', NULL, '11-21-25 She chose the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 7200 to keep the cost down and give some co-pays for some items. SHe''s not thrilled but we can''t go with any alternative options bc of both of the current health issues. She will call to complete the payment in two weeks and cancel the payment with RMHP as well. All set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 16:34:38', '2025-11-21 16:34:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626120', 'Russell Finsterwald', NULL, '11-21-25 Russell called to inquire about professional sports. He''s a professional cyclist! I had no idea. I sent an inquiry to Zion to find out if costs are shareable during training and just not during a Pro event or how they handle pro sports if there''s no insurance kept by the governing body or organizer of the event.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 16:01:11', '2025-11-21 16:01:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175202002', 'Gregory Hubachek', NULL, '11-21-25 Greg didn''t show up for our appt yesterday at 3:00 MST. I left him a vm then and again today now at 3:47. Hopefully I''ll hear back from him again soon.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 15:48:46', '2025-11-21 15:48:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004367112', 'Noah Spencer', NULL, '11-21-25 Left another vm. Playing phone tag with him. He wants to review his membership.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 15:39:44', '2025-11-21 15:39:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000055626120', 'Russell Finsterwald', NULL, '11-21-25 Playing phone tag. Leaving a vm now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 15:39:09', '2025-11-21 15:39:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174239026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178071375', 'Heidi Godsil', NULL, '11-21-25 Heidi and Scott chose to enroll in Secure HSA plud their 21 year old son Max. They chose $1250/$1070 EF for Jan. 1st. They asked a few more great questions.They enrolled via the WWSRA site and I gave them the $100 waived as a member. Heidi is 54, Scott 56 and Max 21. They will fund their current HSA account in 2026. All set for now! Super nice.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-21 15:28:29', '2025-11-21 15:28:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174206191', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028471338', 'Steve Tobias', NULL, '11/21/25<br>Called in having trouble with the portal while he was trying to upload documents to a share request. Also wanted to know the status of an ongoing request so we called up Zion together to see if they could give him some answers and assistance,<br>They mentioned the portal is having a little issues today and not all the documents he uploaded went through. he is going to try and keep uploading them to make sure they get all the info. He is going to make the files smaller to see if it will go through easier. Will also give him the number if he needs to call zion to ask about this as well as let him know he can just call us to transfer or do a 3 way call again to make sure he is good. <br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 14:57:39', '2025-11-21 14:57:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174205067', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059061180', 'William Reyes', NULL, '11/21 member had questions on chat about vaccines  under the ACA. DM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 14:20:20', '2025-11-21 14:20:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174247005', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059061180', 'William Reyes', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat with Concierge', 'Visit ID : 4554 Question : Hi. I''m trying to find out how to get vaccines that are covered under ACA. The Rx plan shows a cost for vaccines which should be "free" under ACA. The Shingles vaccine is over $200 a dose.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-11-21 14:05:14', '2025-11-21 14:05:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174202204', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174273004', 'Phillip Eaton', NULL, 'Member Only $2500 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-11-21 14:01:58', '2025-11-21 14:01:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174206132', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043575167', 'Peggy Neises', NULL, '11/21/25<br>Called in not feeling well and wanting a little guidance. Let her know that she can use the urgent care on the telehealth to try and get some help. Guided her there and showed her how to set up ana ppointment. She is good to go and will reach out if she has any issues.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 13:56:40', '2025-11-21 13:56:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174207266', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103782023', 'Lukas Baker', 'Member & Family $5000 IUA Secure HSA', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-21 13:48:58', '2025-11-21 13:48:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174214089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146467002', 'Meegan Oldani', '11/21', 'went for annual wellness for obgyn, she moved, someone else at facility that might take plan, provider sounded confused, i explained network to her, then got her logged into app and showed her how to use virtual telemental health.', 'Tupac Manzanarez', 'Tupac Manzanarez', '2025-11-21 13:48:31', '2025-11-21 13:48:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174205062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086715002', 'Nancy Krampetz', NULL, '11/21 received a voicemail from 561-223-6319 regarding a billing issue. I called the office back. He was calling for a CPT code from 09/15/2025 for this member. Emailed Lori from ARM for assistance.', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 13:48:18', '2025-11-21 13:48:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174277028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154074002', 'Alexandria Steppe', NULL, '11/21/25 Member requested to cancel membership. Cancellation form e-mailed to her. SW', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 13:45:15', '2025-11-21 13:45:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174206100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123789009', 'Huong Le', NULL, '11/21/25<br>Got referral faxed to his hospital and will be making appointment when they get that. Also looked at the blood test he wanted (JAK 2) and it looks like the price on ultra labs is the cheapest. i can not find any other options lower. <br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-21 13:41:17', '2025-11-21 13:41:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000174202194', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136403002', 'Duane Ellsworth', NULL, 'Member called in and wanted to go over some options for membership.  I directed her to Kirk', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-11-21 13:34:50', '2025-11-21 13:34:50'),
