  ('zcrm_1579374000173974217', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004367112', 'Noah Spencer', NULL, '11-19-25 Left him a vm to review his membership.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 23:10:15', '2025-11-19 23:10:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974212', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110552002', 'Sheryl Hadley', NULL, '11-19-25 Left her a vm to discuss changes with HAB.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 23:09:39', '2025-11-19 23:09:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974204', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176042001', 'Harry Bowers II', NULL, '11-19-25 Melissa is 57, Lee 59 and son Zeeland, 17 and turning 18 in Jan 2026. They live in Marble, CO and have been involved with the Lead King Loop. Lee has been on ski patrol for years but no longer. They were avid skiers but doing more back country now due to crowds and such. They watched the video. They won''t be getting an APTC and their monthly cost is going to $3500 for family!! They have a DPC membership. Melissa is the only one with some health issues. She has Hashimotos that they are getting help with via the DPC since traditional care doesn''t really acknowledge it. The meds are cheap for it. She has a possible pinched nerve in her neck that she''s getting looked at on Dec. 8th. We are talking again on the 11th. Depending on the outcome of the visit will determine if she sticks with C4 or moves to MCS. She also has a tiny benign mengionoma in her brain. They found it by accident and it''s never changed in the years they''ve been watching it. If it comes back with no change again they will only watch it every 5 years moving forward. She''s and her dr. are really not worried about it. She could have had it all of her life or for a very long time. It hasn''t caused any symptoms or needed any treatment of any kind ever. The only thing Lee has is high cholesterol. They are mostly retired but have a rental property and will qualify for Secure HSA or they might choose Care+ since they are already paying for a DPC. They will decide. Daughter is totally healthy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 22:49:14', '2025-12-11 09:22:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974184', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000135858012', 'Jessica Vollmer', NULL, '11-19-25  For her possible renewal it''s showing no APTC but $80 from CAP! When I do a test outside of her account the $80 doesn''s show up. Not sure if this is a mistake with C4. So, I don''t want toremove the auto renew in case she loses the $80. <br><span><br></span><p style="background-color:rgb(0, 100, 71);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(252, 252, 252);background-color:rgb(0, 100, 71);"><b>Current plan</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><br></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><b>Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><b>$372.18 </b></span><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);">/ month</span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><i>after $0.00 financial help</i></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(0, 100, 71);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(252, 252, 252);background-color:rgb(0, 100, 71);"><b>Renewal Plan</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><br></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><b>Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0</b></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><b>$387.65 </b></span><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);">/ month</span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><i>after $80.00 financial help</i></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);"><br></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(33, 37, 41);background-color:rgb(252, 252, 252);">That said, she''s interested in lowering cost even more with Care+ and I sent her information about maternity with her current Cigna plan and with Care+. She knows about the 6 month waiting period which she''s not concerned about. She''s 30 and might refer her boyfriend to me as well. She has W2 only for income, hence the Care+ choice. She knows of $125/$25 as well. She will review it all and let me know.</span></p>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 22:28:12', '2025-11-19 22:28:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974160', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173974142', 'Solomon Liston', NULL, '11-19-25 I accidentally put this under contacts instead of leads. Solomon came via Willa Bonzi. He''s exploring ALL options including Zion directly, Sedera directly or through SALA or through his local chamber. He''s 47 and he''s newly married to his husband who is 41. They can''t do Medishare bc they won''t honor their marriage. They have a RMHP/UHC plan now for only $50 for the two of them. They will go up to $1500 in 2026. They are working with their accountant to determine the best way to handle their situation sinc they will likely have to pay $ back in taxes for 2025.  Solomon is healthy. His husband is a personal trainer. But, he has digestive issues and Krohn''s disease. Solomon faced paying $600 for his wellness visit this year bc there were non preventive items on the bill it sounds like.I educated him about how to manage that moving forward. He''s been very displeased with the level of service with UHC. They are looking at a Jan. 1st start date. They are also reviewing Sharewell. I gave him my thoughts on that. Also, one of the entities is offering E-Benefits in addition. I think Sharewell is doing that.  If he gets the membership through Sala, he says the equivalent looks to be around $200 cheaper!  He would have to pay a 1x $200 fee to join Sala''s association. We discussed all 4 memberships, Care+, Secure HSA and both Premium memberships. He''s most interested in Care+ and Premium Care at this point He also has a membership with Trailhead DPC. So, he likely won''t make use of the virtual healthcare app. He can get a colonoscopy through Trailhead Clinic''s partner in GJ for $1200-$1500!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 22:02:13', '2025-11-19 22:02:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974137', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174010038', 'Daniel Koerber', NULL, '11-19-25 Dan is Michelle Skellion''s boyfriend and referred by her. He''s 35. He''s been on C4. Something he mentioned is $650. His Bronze plan is going to $430. He has no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. His aunt also does health sharing. We discussed Care+ since he needs the cost down and he''s young, not needing high cost wellness. He likes the idea of $2500/$216. He joined already and is super thrilled.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 21:47:13', '2025-11-19 21:47:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173992018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141578002', 'Anthony Bertasi', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 4538 Question : How do I setup my account so that my wife can manage the children’s medical needs etc on our MPB health/HSA secure accounts?', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-11-19 21:25:44', '2025-11-19 21:25:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155206002', 'Kellie Matticks', NULL, '11-19-25 Kellie will keep her Premium Care membership. She doesn''t have any sort of self-employment income. She''s fine with Premium Care. She''ll use the HAB for a mammo and colonoscopy before it ends. She already did a well check. She did a vision screening, dental cleanings as well which she will submit for reimbursement. She''s all set for now as long as she can access her email account again successfully. She has a problem with it at the moment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 17:20:16', '2025-11-19 17:20:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974099', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021695264', 'Lorie Moreno-Roch', NULL, '11-19-25 Lorie called to update their address back to Louisville but the system won''t allow it. We''ve rescheduled for Dec. to update address and choose an option for Stephen (SR), Lincoln and Lorie. Stephen (son) and Christian (daughter) are in out of state schools and could be served well with L--X. She said they''d be open to completing the surveys and are definitely healthy. I will send her the questionnaire and some info to review.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 17:05:29', '2025-11-19 22:57:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173974094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044575094', 'Doug Klof', NULL, '11-19-25 Doug is second guessing going to the exchange for his family. Now he''s thinking of putting Heather Klof, his wife onto this as well. Just wants to understand the pre-x clause again before deciding. I left him a vm. I also sent him an email with a copy of the pre-x clause to read through.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-19 16:37:35', '2025-11-19 21:32:16'),
